{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/860555-keeping-kinfolk-clear-of-wyrm-taint","id":860555,"title":"Keeping kinfolk clear of Wyrm taint","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-06T14:31:12-07:00","id":860555,"title":"Keeping kinfolk clear of Wyrm taint","content":"How to keep ones kinfolk clear of wyrm taint, in particular how to not seem like a tyrant when telling your kid &quot;You cant have that toy/Watch That TV show/ go to this or that place&quot; (Because you know its tainted)<br /> <br /> adult kin will hopefully be more understanding and grateful kids... arent as rational.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T19:27:18-07:00","id":860724,"title":"","content":"I think most Garou aren't all that invested in their children on a day-to-day basis. A lot of Garou only show up from time to time to make a periodic contribution of genetic material, and otherwise don't really care what the Kin (or their kids) are doing. Indeed, some Garou intentionally keep their Kin as much in the dark as possible, don't really care if they take an entirely human spouse, and then hit them with Animal Magnetism in order to get them in the sack. Presumably birth control is another contributing factor why the Garou population is crashing in the 20th century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:23:55-07:00","id":860934,"title":"","content":"I think there are plenty of parents, who control what their kids do, or eat, or watch on TV. Possibly they don't even own a TV. If kin is aware and partly involved in garou affairs they will steer clear of wyrm-ish influences as best as they can. Just like parents who are vegetarians, or vegans, have certain religious beliefs and dress accordingly (no trousers for girls, for example) and so on. Human society accepts that. So, it isn't that difficult.<br /> <br /> I would think, that a majority of garou still cares for their kids (and spouses) just as any other person would. They just can't be with them 24/7, so they are more akin to a family with one parent who is deployed or has to travel a lot for work. Basically a long-distance relationship situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T06:09:42-07:00","id":860998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/860555-keeping-kinfolk-clear-of-wyrm-taint#post860555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to keep ones kinfolk clear of wyrm taint, in particular how to not seem like a tyrant when telling your kid &quot;You cant have that toy/Watch That TV show/ go to this or that place&quot; (Because you know its tainted)<br /> <br /> adult kin will hopefully be more understanding and grateful kids... arent as rational.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conveniently, all toys are tainted, all shows are tainted, and all places are tainted except the Caernheart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:40:31-07:00","id":861032,"title":"","content":"The Nocker Toymakers Guild , according to the Nocker Kithbook (which I glanced over at a friends house) is coming under fire from Avalon, for creating toys that dont psychicly corrupt children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:56:37-07:00","id":861115,"title":"","content":"I'll speak a bit from personal experience on this.<br /> <br /> My faith focuses a lot on ritual/spiritual purity. The list of things that can turn you ritually impure is kind of insanely long, and is completely impossible to actually avoid all of no matter how hard you try (since the list includes specific involuntary bodily functions).<br /> <br /> Culturally this doesn't create some sort of inane monastic drive to live in absolute seclusion, it creates common rituals of purification. Just like physical hygiene, you're going to get dirty no matter how hard you try not to, so you develop ways to clean yourself off.<br /> <br /> One of the reason to keep up your dues with your local religious institution in this context is to fund the maintenance and have access to the materials necessary for doing this when you need to. Even if you're not particularly observant, or religious, as long as you're in good standing you can schedule a spiritual cleansing one a regular basis just to be safe.<br /> <br /> Translating that to the cultures of long standing kin families with at least some members in the know is pretty simple. While not in the books (something that seems a bit of an oversight, but whatever), it should be fairly simple to have a minor Rite that exists to expel the minor taint that builds up slowly like dirt under your nails without having to wait for enough taint to bother with the full Rite of Cleansing. You then encourage this minor Rite (even if it doesn't actually spiritually cleanse kin without a Garou doing it) as a family practice among kin families as a regular monthly thing they do. Then you try to show up at least one every month or two with a Garou, and they do the minor Rite, and the little bits of spiritual cruft that builds up is removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:27:13-07:00","id":861133,"title":"","content":"Are you Jewish or shinto? Thought id ask , been dabbling with shinto last 3 years or so, and read the old testament when I was in my preteens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T12:58:54-07:00","id":861225,"title":"","content":"I think the corruption paragraph in 2nd mentioned, that living a gaia-pleasing life style will remove all taint over time, so that it can't turn into permanent corruption. No special rites (not even minor ones) necessary. And if this is true for garou, who make it a habit to savagely kill stuff on occasions, then it is true for kin and humans, too. <br /> Meaning, if you lead a &quot;normal&quot; live (spiritually balanced, that is) all taint you acquire will fade away on it's own... only if you acquire more than your lifestyle can handle, you are on a downwards spiral...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:32:37-07:00","id":861311,"title":"","content":"Interesting perspective, Heavy Arms. I think that taint should be related to individual choice. A person making compromises they know are harmful for themselves and others, surrendering in a moment of weakness to dark desires... I don't really like how TV programs or evil toys produced by Pentex make people into monsters; I find it cartoonish and simplistic. Falling into the Wyrm's clutches because you ate the wrong brand of Cheerios this morning is pretty silly.<br /> <br /> There can be exceptions to this, but generally I think it is unhelpful to the overall feel of the game if innocents are in constant danger of being tainted. I want sense taint to be at least somewhat useful as a heuristic, if not the be-all-end-all way of determining who is friend or foe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 04-07-2016, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:48:06-07:00","id":861385,"title":"","content":"Others could argue it keeps things from getting too simplistic for the PC's as &quot;Taint&quot; Doesnt imply &quot;Needs to die&quot; <br /> <br /> a rape victim will be tainted just like the rapist...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:02:56-07:00","id":861393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/860555-keeping-kinfolk-clear-of-wyrm-taint?p=861385#post861385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Others could argue it keeps things from getting too simplistic for the PC's as &quot;Taint&quot; Doesnt imply &quot;Needs to die&quot;<br /> <br /> a rape victim will be tainted just like the rapist...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in my game they won't. Psychological damage =/= Wyrm taint. Those who embrace the Wyrm are often not in their right mind, but that doesn't mean those with neuroses or psychoses are tainted by defacto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T17:17:39-07:00","id":861449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/860555-keeping-kinfolk-clear-of-wyrm-taint?p=861133#post861133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you Jewish or shinto?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jewish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/860555-keeping-kinfolk-clear-of-wyrm-taint?p=861311#post861311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that taint should be related to individual choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate your desires here, but it isn't the baseline of the game. Taint (and not just Wyrm taint) is a metaphysical &quot;dirt.&quot; You get dirty by being alive in the world. You can live a life that reduces the dirt as much as possible, you can choose to slog through the mud and have to shower a lot, or you can hallow in the dirt.<br /> <br /> I think regardless of how one gets taint, this differentiation is important. A small moral lapse can't be as bad for you as a major one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want sense taint to be at least somewhat useful as a heuristic, if not the be-all-end-all way of determining who is friend or foe. </div> </div> </div>There isn't a &quot;sense taint&quot; though. There are Sense Wyrm/Weaver/Wyld Gifts. Something that is fairly important to the baseline setting, is there is a difference between &quot;tainted&quot; individuals and entities that are inherently part of that essence. Banes aren't &quot;Wyrm-tainted spirits,&quot; they are Wyrm-spirits as an essential aspect of their natures. Part of the ambiguity of Sense Wyrm is that it doesn't directly translate the divide there. A Wyrm-tainted cop that's picked up taint by choosing to dip into drugs to have the energy to keep up with the crushing weight of their workload, and a bane, both are sensed as being &quot;of the Wyrm,&quot; even if the cop could be cleansed and saved - and still has a core moral good worth saving - while the bane is a bane until you break out things like certain Rank 5 powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T18:14:05-07:00","id":861479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/860555-keeping-kinfolk-clear-of-wyrm-taint?p=861449#post861449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate your desires here, but it isn't the baseline of the game. Taint (and not just Wyrm taint) is a metaphysical &quot;dirt.&quot; You get dirty by being alive in the world. You can live a life that reduces the dirt as much as possible, you can choose to slog through the mud and have to shower a lot, or you can hallow in the dirt.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I reject that, absolutely. It is neither interesting or particularly useful as a narrative standpoint. The Wyrm may be nearly ubiquitous, but it is not in all things; it is in the WORST things. Not all who are insane are tainted, nor are all who hate or pollute. I don''t think it should be easy to become tainted by the Wyrm- and maybe that is just my personal spin on the setting. I can accept that. I think a lot of the Pentex stuff is hilariously campy bullshit. Cars that spread taint, toys that spread taint, medicine that spreads taint, it is hokey and reeks of the Captain Planet garbage villainy that people complain about, and rightly so.<br /> <br /> I don't want my werewolves to be threatened by dolls.<br /> <br /> Now, to be clear, I think the idea of, say, Gorehounds getting their head start by watching too many horror movies is a bit silly, but I am even ok with that as long as it isn't due to a specific cursed, bane-infused DVD. Fastening onto the idea of violence as virtue and fantasizing about slaughtering innocents... that is a great crack in the soul that the Wyrm might wriggle into. I think everyone has the capacity to become tainted, to give in to the darkness, but that should require at least a small degree of personal agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T18:57:41-07:00","id":861512,"title":"","content":"You can reject it all you want... but that doesn't change the way the game is written.<br /> <br /> As well, I don't find the idea that the Wyrm is only &quot;in the worst things,&quot; interesting or useful. That is the path to campy bullshit, because it removes all ambiguity and nuance. Wyrm = purely evil. This both rejects the concept of the Triat as ideally being in everything in balance; that Taint is an imbalance between them more than anything else.<br /> <br /> Does the Pentex material often take things too far? Sure. But it's been ~23 years or so, with multiple editions, with multiple developers and writers, with multiple tones. The problem with Pentex is not how taint works metaphysically in WtA, but the presentation and tone of the way Pentex is presented.<br /> <br /> Werewolves aren't threatened by dolls. Wyrm taint spreading dolls represent a problem that is a challenge to the Garou. It's a subversive enemy corrupting humans and kinfolk quietly. It's not a foe you can face in battle. It's an enemy that flies in the face of traditional Garou notions of their role as warriors and their cultural biases towards problems with the Wyrm. It's an evolution of the Wyrm servants' tactics that gives the Glasswalkers, Bone Gnawers, and Children of Gaia purpose in the war to fight on an unconventional level.<br /> <br /> Forcing the Wyrm into a narrative role that only works when people (not necessarily without duress or while fully informed) &quot;consent&quot; to the Wyrm's urges removes a lot of the tools of the Wyrm in the war. The Wyrm can't be toxic metaphysically if its poisonous urges are defeated by just saying no.<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> In general a few points beyond that:<br /> <br /> First, this applies to all of the Triat, not just the Wyrm. I understand why we're focusing on Wyrm-taint, but the metaphysics of taint in the books-as-written apply to all three types. That consistency shapes how taint needs to work on a narrative level. It might open up the space for gonzo Wyrm silliness, but it is also part of how Wyld and Weaver taint can remain relevant.<br /> <br /> Second, please stop conflating mental illness into this. Nobody is saying that mental illness makes you tainted. The closest was a comment that trauma can be an avenue through which taint is spread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T19:52:58-07:00","id":861550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/860555-keeping-kinfolk-clear-of-wyrm-taint?p=861512#post861512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can reject it all you want... but that doesn't change the way the game is written.<br /> <br /> <br /> Forcing the Wyrm into a narrative role that only works when people (not necessarily without duress or while fully informed) &quot;consent&quot; to the Wyrm's urges removes a lot of the tools of the Wyrm in the war. The Wyrm can't be toxic metaphysically if its poisonous urges are defeated by just saying no.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Amen, Heavy Arms, Amen!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T00:47:02-07:00","id":861664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/860555-keeping-kinfolk-clear-of-wyrm-taint?p=861449#post861449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taint (and not just Wyrm taint) is a metaphysical &quot;dirt.&quot; You get dirty by being alive in the world. You can live a life that reduces the dirt as much as possible, you can choose to slog through the mud and have to shower a lot, or you can hallow in the dirt.<br /> <br /> I think regardless of how one gets taint, this differentiation is important. A small moral lapse can't be as bad for you as a major one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that analogy.<br /> The important thing is, that there is a difference between &quot;taint&quot; and &quot;corruption&quot;. A corrupted being acquires new taint through his actions. A person who was only tainted will, depending on her lifestyle, loose the taint over time. That is why the information granted by &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; alone isn't enough to judge a person - although enough successes might give one a pretty good idea, if a person/object/place is tainted or corrupt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is neither interesting or particularly useful as a narrative standpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>But from a narrative standpoint, there should be something for the players left to investigate. The moral dilemma, whether or not a person need to be killed or is worth the extra mile to be saved is a big part of the game. If Wyrm-Taint was to be present only with the already corrupted beings, I think the game would be all to easy - and ultimately boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:44:30-07:00","id":861791,"title":"","content":"Really like the side note in the 3rd edition corebook (started right before it was released mind you) &quot;Its not detect evil&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:52:33-07:00","id":861795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/860555-keeping-kinfolk-clear-of-wyrm-taint?p=861664#post861664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that analogy.<br /> The important thing is, that there is a difference between &quot;taint&quot; and &quot;corruption&quot;. A corrupted being acquires new taint through his actions. A person who was only tainted will, depending on her lifestyle, loose the taint over time. That is why the information granted by &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; alone isn't enough to judge a person - although enough successes might give one a pretty good idea, if a person/object/place is tainted or corrupt.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the difference between &quot;dirt&quot; and &quot;filth&quot;.<br /> <br /> IME, Sense Wyrm has several levels of response:<br /> 0: Clean and Pure, like in the Caernheart or just after a Rite of Cleansing.<br /> 1: The normal everyday taint you get from living in a world with global climate destabilization, chlorinated tapwater, gasoline engines, pesticides, etc.<br /> 2: The normal everyday taint you get from living in the more rundown parts of cities where sanitation and the police are scare, with crime, drugs, lead pipes, and asbestos insulation are common.<br /> 3: Exposure to freaky Wyrm shit, like having taken tainted drugs, drunk kindred vitae, performed abominable acts, etc. These people/things spread the taint around but not necessarily consciously. Curable Fomori, tainted nature spirits, Thrall of the Wyrm, scorched earth style greed and revenge.<br /> 4: Leading or encouraging freaky Wyrm shit, deliberately but still not necessarily knowingly. Banes, Corrupted Fera, Pentex Corporate Officers. Even some of these are still curable.<br /> 5: Actively serving and delighting in the Wyrm's corruption. Wyrm Totems, high ranking BSDs, slaughterhouses of the innocent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","user":"etherial","date":". 04-11-2016, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:40:06-07:00","id":862740,"title":"","content":"do agree a garou probaly can detect the strength of the wyrms stench.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T02:11:42-07:00","id":863536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/860555-keeping-kinfolk-clear-of-wyrm-taint?p=862740#post862740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do agree a garou probaly can detect the strength of the wyrms stench.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that is what every success after the first is good for, on an activation roll.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> I' go with something like that...<ul><li>Is there 'dirt' in the area ?</li> <li>Is it on a specific person/object or the general scene?</li> <li>Is the dirt 'normal', and going away on it's own over time, or is it something deeper, like a red wine stain...?</li> <li>What is the reason for the taint (vague information) ?</li> <li>Is the 'dirt' excessive or minor ?</li> </ul><br /> Depending on successes, situation and plot requirements I'd pick informations from such a list and tell the player who used the gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 04-11-2016, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T11:05:18-07:00","id":863775,"title":"","content":"Re: wyrm taint being 'willing' or not, I do think we'd mostly all agree that if a kid picks up some horrifying Tellus-made skinhead simulator because Grand Theft Auto is too tame is going to start getting tainted by how warped it makes them, no matter how much they assert that video games don't cause violence. (Aren't fictional worlds fun?) Lots of Pentex products just quietly nudge people into making bad decisions. Advertising for beauty products tries to change the social narrative to something shallow and jealous, making people more receptive; O'Tolley's pushes people towards gluttony, excess and apathy. All normal pretty uncontroversial stuff.<br /> <br /> I think it's kinda like gardening though. There's plants seeds everywhere, seeds everywhere, if you have dirt then something's going to grow eventually. But if you want to grow something specific, you prepare the soil and plant the seeds you want. A lot of Wyrm-tainted corporations first mess with peoples' heads, and then find ways to get Banes directly to the consumer. There's spirits all over the place all the time, but if you want something specific, and you want something insidious, and you want it NOW, then you attach a little something extra to that Botox treatment, or you add a secret ingredient to your O'Nuggets, or you put a _really_ special prize with that extra-rare card in the CCG booster deck, where the people most likely to be open to its influence are the ones who wind up with it.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Your Kinfolk won't suddenly turn evil just from buying King Beer. Your pack is probably justified not caring if your Ahroun downs a pack. But King Distilleries pushes alcoholism more than your average label, and if someone IS alcoholic and violent, they're more likely to get screwed over from a Wyrm tainted brand. Keep your Kinfolk morally and ethically clean and you don't have to worry much; who cares if your pre-change kid plays GTA as long as you teach him video games aren't reality. But when someone is really teetering on the edge, like everyone is sometimes, be careful what brand of Cheerios they eat, and maybe pop into the Umbra once in a while to make sure there's no monkey on their back. I mean, you can get those things anywhere. Some physical locations have more Banes than others, and Pentex wants those places to include your living room.<br /> <br /> That's the way I'm used to seeing it, anyway.<br /> <br /> (Unless it's that comic from the Nuwisha book, with the train that just shoves Banes into perfectly upstanding human beings. I mean, there's some insanely nasty big-bad spirit juju going on there at the time, but if Pentex could do that all the time, they'd find a good strategy to do that once in a while.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:23:43-07:00","id":864073,"title":"","content":"Wyrm taint can be seen as a kind of spiritual pollution. That pollution can be caused by people's own choices and decisions, but it also exists for reasons that have nothing to do with moral choices. Someone choosing to commit evil acts produces that pollution. Toxic chemicals that destroy the environment also causes that spiritual pollution. A natural volcano that spews all sorts of toxic fumes and sulfur into the atmosphere also produces that spiritual pollution. A meteor from space carrying the Andromeda Strain produces that pollution.<br /> <br /> Each of these cases are completely different from each other, but resolving the Wyrm Taint they cause call for completely different adventures. I think this is a strength as it allows the ST and players to run the kind of game that is fun for them. We can keep things very simple for the PCs. Or introduce moral dilemmas. Or require them to think about how to solve a problem that cannot be resolved by killing a bad guy.<br /> <br /> I always refer to Wyrm Taint as a kind of miasma. In Greek mythology, a miasma is a &quot;contagious power&quot; that has a life of its own. Until purged by the sacrificial death of the wrongdoer, society would be chronically infected by catastrophe. This later gave its name to the miasmal theory of disease which explained that certain diseases were a result of &quot;bad air&quot; that were emitted at night and created epidemics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}